# Remix Development Guidelines

## Project Structure

1. Follow the Remix file-based routing convention:
   - Place route components in `app/routes`
   - Use the `$` prefix for dynamic segments
   - Use `_` prefix for layout routes
   - Use `.` for nested routes

2. Data Flow:
```typescript
// Good - Loader function
export async function loader({ request, params }: LoaderArgs) {
  return json({ data: await getData(params.id) });
}

// Good - Action function
export async function action({ request }: ActionArgs) {
  const formData = await request.formData();
  return json(await processData(formData));
}
```

3. Error Handling:
```typescript
// Good - Error Boundary
export function ErrorBoundary({ error }: { error: Error }) {
  return (
    <div className="error-container">
      <h1>Error</h1>
      <p>{error.message}</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

4. Resource Routes:
- Place resource routes in `app/routes/resources/`
- Use for API endpoints and non-UI routes

5. Models and Services:
- Place data models in `app/models/`
- Place services in `app/services/`
- Keep business logic separate from components

6. Performance:
- Use `prefetch="intent"` for anticipated navigations
- Implement optimistic UI updates
- Use `headers` export for proper caching

## Common Patterns

1. Form Submissions:
```typescript
// Good
export default function MyForm() {
  return (
    <Form method="post">
      <input type="text" name="title" required />
      <button type="submit">Submit</button>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

2. Data Loading:
```typescript
// Good - Using useLoaderData
export default function Route() {
  const { data } = useLoaderData<typeof loader>();
  return <div>{data.title}</div>;
}
```

3. Client-Side Navigation:
```typescript
// Good
import { Link } from "@remix-run/react";

export default function Navigation() {
  return (
    <Link to="/posts" prefetch="intent">
      View Posts
    </Link>
  );
}
``` 